@title Tallgrass Telemetry Pipeline
@subtitle Windspire Energy, Tallgrass wind farm
@author Asset Performance
@date 2026-10-06

# Overview
Turbine data is collected on site and summarized before it is sent to the operations cloud over a limited link. The grid operator receives output and availability figures directly from the site.

!! On satellite fallback the Control Room sees one-minute averages, not full-resolution data. The Edge Historian holds up to 72 hours of full-resolution data until the fiber link returns.

# Pipeline
diagram pipe dir=TB title="Telemetry pipeline"
pipe: turbines "Turbine Controllers" svc "62 turbines"
pipe: scada "Site SCADA" svc focus
pipe: hist "Edge Historian" store "72 h buffer" focus
pipe: gw "Ingest Gateway" svc
pipe: tsdb "Time-Series Store" db
pipe: fc "Forecast Service" svc
pipe: grid "Grid Operator" ext
pipe: room "Control Room" team
pipe: turbines -> scada : 1 sample/s
pipe: scada -> hist : buffered storage
pipe: scada -> grid : every 4 s
pipe: hist --> gw : compressed batches
pipe: gw -> tsdb : validated samples
pipe: tsdb -> fc : history
pipe: fc -> room : 24 h forecast
pipe: tsdb -> room : live and historical
pipe: group site "Tallgrass Site" turbines, scada, hist
pipe: group cloud "Windspire Operations Cloud" gw, tsdb, fc
pipe: legend

The site sends output and availability to the Grid Operator every 4 seconds. The Edge Historian sends compressed batches to the cloud over fiber, or over satellite when fiber is down.

# Sizing
kpi Turbines | 62 | 140 signals each
kpi Sample rate | 8,680/s
kpi Daily volume | ~750M samples
kpi Edge buffer | 72 h | full resolution

table = item,value; Full-resolution retention,30 days; One-minute average retention,5 years; Fiber link,100 Mbps (full resolution); Satellite fallback,2 Mbps (one-minute averages only)
